cpp/src/fe_modifiers.cpp - fe_mod_laplacian_smooth()
  Ported from  source/blender/modifiers/intern/MOD_laplaciansmooth.cc
  Upstream     blender/blender @ e240930f046045145f0e03ba237caa7192ccf449
  Copyright    2005-2023 Blender Authors
  Licence      GPL-2.0-or-later (this repository distributes it under
               GPL-3.0-or-later, which the "or later" clause permits)
  What         init_laplacian_matrix(), fill_laplacian_matrix() and
               validate_solution(): the cotangent ring operator, the
               scale-dependent umbrella on boundary vertices, the vweights /
               vlengths normalisation, the min_area zerola pinning, the signed
               blend-back of the solution and volume_preservation(). Upstream
               solves the least-squares system with Eigen's
               LeastSquaresConjugateGradient; that solver is not linkable from a
               freestanding module, so the same normal equations are solved
               with conjugate gradients and a Jacobi preconditioner instead.
               Not ported: vertex-group weighting.

cpp/src/fe_modifiers.cpp - fe_mod_edge_split()
  Ported from  source/blender/modifiers/intern/MOD_edgesplit.cc and
               source/blender/bmesh/tools/bmesh_edgesplit.cc
  Upstream     blender/blender @ e240930f046045145f0e03ba237caa7192ccf449
  Copyright    2005-2023 Blender Authors
  Licence      GPL-2.0-or-later (this repository distributes it under
               GPL-3.0-or-later, which the "or later" clause permits)
  What         doEdgeSplit()'s seam rule - the cosf(split_angle + 1.75e-7)
               threshold, the "3 or more faces" case and the split-everything
               case - then BM_mesh_edgesplit() / BM_vert_separate_hflag() in
               the form a triangle buffer needs: the faces around each vertex
               are grouped into the fans still joined by unsplit edges, and
               every fan gets its own copy of that vertex and its UV. Not
               ported literally: MOD_EDGESPLIT_FROMFLAG's sharp edges, because
               this pipeline stores one smooth flag per face, not per edge. The
               Sharp Edges option splits at the shading boundary instead - the
               edge between a flat face and a smooth one - which is the sharp
               edge such a mesh actually carries.
